   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# regions from id renders\n\n1. `folder`: the render folder with `ids_<pass>.png` + `ids_<pass>.txt` (`<name> rgb r g b`, linear like Houdini writes them) and optional full-res `mask_<name>.exr` (alpha; `png/mask_<name>.png` as fallback).\n2. `regions_pass = elements`: every element is a region, separate parts numbered in reading order (`windows_01..`, `split_parts`). Other passes (`zone`, `level`, `bay`) become tags.\n3. `overlap = id_map`: object masks ignore occlusion, the ID map decides what is in front (depth order in the report). `smaller_wins` brings hidden details back (the recessed clock).\n4. Rules: `[group:windows tag:level_1]`, `[tag:zone_left]`, `[tag:bay_3]`.\n\ntest: 17 elements, 4 passes, 365 regions (280 glass panes) in 12 s; full-res result agrees with the half-res ID map on 98 % of interior pixels.\n"
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
